ognition of the kernel argument.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2604.01975:I005","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_operation_step_or_formula","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2604.01975:I005:U001","2604.01975:I005:U002","2604.01975:I005:U005"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U002","ISSUE-001:U006"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue concerns the incorrect kernel inclusion in the GE-PI half-matrix proof. ISSUE-001 concerns the range and step size of labels in an SU(2) dimension recurrence; the prediction does not identify the GE-PI kernel defect.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2604.01975:I007","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2604.01975:I007:U001","2604.01975:I007:U003","2604.01975:I007:U006"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U002","ISSUE-001:U006"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is the false inference from infinitesimal kernel conditions to global equivariance for a scalar linear combination of representation entries, requiring an integration-of-intertwiners argument. ISSUE-001 addresses only SU(2) label indexing in a dimension formula and does not recognize this representation-theoretic sufficiency failure.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]}]